{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.KashiwaraCrystalBasic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.KashiwaraCrystalBasic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":42,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instCompositeKashiwaraResidueAStandardSl2Crystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instCompositeKashiwaraResidueAStandardSl2Crystal","kind":"instance","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L362-L372","doc":"**`B(Λ₁)` inhabits `CompositeKashiwaraResidueA`**: it is a Stembridge\ncrystal, carries a type-A embedding (`n = 2`) and a Demazure sub-crystal\n(`level = 1`).  The explicit `.{0,0}` universe annotation pins the two\nuniverse metavariables introduced by the universe-carrying `TypeACrystal`/\n`DemazureSubcrystal` target fields (§7d — `standardSl2Crystal.V = Bool`\nand each abstract `target.V` live in `Type 0`), so the three base instances\nunify at a single rigid universe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.has_demazure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.has_demazure","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L353-L353","doc":"Demazure sub-crystal correspondence at some level (`Nonempty` for the\nsame reason). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.has_type_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.has_type_A","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L350-L350","doc":"Type-A specialisation at some n (data class, so wrapped in `Nonempty`\nto sit inside the existential). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.is_stembridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.is_stembridge","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L347-L347","doc":"Stembridge axioms hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA.mk","kind":"ctor","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L345-L345","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CompositeKashiwaraResidueA","kind":"class","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L343-L353","doc":"Conditional class combining the three classes above for the\ncomposite identification of residue A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.sl3_singleton_not_closed_at_level_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.sl3_singleton_not_closed_at_level_one","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L321-L333","doc":"**…and it constrains the predicate at a fixed level, too (PROVED).**  The\nsingleton `{0}` — which *is* the level-0 Demazure sub-crystal `B_e(Λ₁)` — is not\nclosed at `level = 1`, because `f₀` carries `0` to `1`.  Together with\n`sl3DemazureLevelOne` this pins the field down from both sides: at a fixed level\nit selects which subsets are Demazure sub-crystals, and for a fixed subset it\nselects which levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.sl3LevelOne_not_closed_at_level_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.sl3LevelOne_not_closed_at_level_two","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L304-L319","doc":"**`demazure_closure` is a falsifiable condition (PROVED).**  The very same\nmembership predicate `{0, 1}` fails the closure requirement at `level = 2`,\nbecause `f₁` carries `1` to `2`, which is outside it.  So the strengthened field\nis not `True` in disguise: it holds at level 1 and fails at level 2 for one fixed\npredicate — which is what `member ≡ True` could never show. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.sl3DemazureLevelOne_proper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.sl3DemazureLevelOne_proper","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L298-L302","doc":"**The sub-crystal really is proper (PROVED)**: the lowest vertex `2` is not a\nmember, so this witness is not the whole crystal in disguise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.sl3DemazureLevelOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.sl3DemazureLevelOne","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L273-L296","doc":"**A PROPER Demazure sub-crystal**: `B_{s₀}(Λ₁) = {0, 1}` inside the\nthree-vertex `sl₃` crystal, at `level = 1`.\n\nUnlike `instSl2DemazureSubcrystal`, `demazure_closure` here is a real obligation:\nthe membership predicate excludes the vertex `2`, so the proof has to check that\nno `f₀`-arrow leaves `{0, 1}` — none does, because the only arrow out of `1` is\n`f₁`, which `level = 1` does not range over.\n\nDeliberately a `def` and not an `instance`: nothing should acquire this witness\nby resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.standardSl3Crystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.standardSl3Crystal","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L252-L271","doc":"The **standard `sl₃` crystal** `B(Λ₁)`: three vertices in a string\n`0 -f₀→ 1 -f₁→ 2`, with the matching `e`-inverses.  Vertex `0` is the\nhighest-weight vector; there are two simple roots, labelled `0` and `1`.\n\nAn `abbrev` rather than a `def` (unlike `standardSl2Crystal`) so that\n`standardSl3Crystal.V` reduces to `Fin 3` at *reducible* transparency and\ninstance search finds `OfNat` / `DecidableEq` / `Fintype` on the vertices — which\nis what lets the closure obligations below be discharged by `decide`.  The `sl₂`\ncrystal needs none of this: its vertices are `Bool`, whose two literals are\nconstructors rather than numerals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instSl2DemazureSubcrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instSl2DemazureSubcrystal","kind":"instance","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L212-L243","doc":"**`B(Λ₁)`'s level-1 Demazure sub-crystal — which happens to be everything.**\n\n`sl₂` has one simple root, so `W = {e, s₀}` and `B(Λ₁)` has exactly two Demazure\nsub-crystals: `B_e(Λ₁) = {u_Λ}` at length 0, and\n`B_{s₀}(Λ₁) = {u_Λ, f₀ u_Λ}` at length 1 — and the second is the *whole*\ntwo-vertex crystal.  So `member := fun _ => True` is the **correct value** here,\nnot a shortcut: the level-1 sub-crystal of `B(Λ₁)` really is all of it.\n\n**What that costs, and why it was flagged** (2026-08-24, bean `qou-uno5`).  This\ndocstring used to call the witness *\"a genuine `DemazureSubcrystal` … closed\nunder lowering\"*, which reads as though closure had been checked.  It has not:\nwith `member ≡ True` both the hypothesis and the conclusion of\n`demazure_closure` are trivially inhabited, so the field closes by `trivial` —\nexactly the strength it had when it was literally `True`, before someone\nstrengthened it into the real closure condition.  The strengthening bought\nnothing *while this was the only inhabitant*.  It is not any more:\n`sl3DemazureLevelOne` below is a **proper** sub-crystal whose closure has to be\nverified, and `sl3LevelOne_not_closed_at_level_two` proves the field can fail.\n\n`highest_isHighest` is the one field this witness does exercise — `e i false =\nnone` for every `i` is checked, not assumed.\n\nStill a global `instance`, and correctly so: `DemazureSubcrystal\nstandardSl2Crystal 1` is a fact about a concrete two-vertex crystal, not a\nconjecture, so resolution supplying it is sound.  Read it as \"the whole crystal\nat the longest Weyl word\", never as evidence about Demazure closure in general. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instSl2TypeACrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instSl2TypeACrystal","kind":"instance","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L201-L210","doc":"**`B(Λ₁)` is a genuine `TypeACrystal`** at `n = 2`: it embeds into the\nstandard `sl₂` crystal (itself) by the identity, which is a crystal\nmorphism (commutes with `f`/`e`) and is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_closure","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L191-L191","doc":"**Demazure closure** (was `True`): the sub-crystal is closed under\nlowering by the first `level` simple roots — exactly the operators\nin the support of the length-`level` Weyl word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest_isHighest","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest_isHighest","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L187-L187","doc":"`highest` really is highest-weight: every raising operator\nannihilates it (`e i highest = none`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest_mem","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L184-L184","doc":"The generator lies in the sub-crystal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.highest","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L182-L182","doc":"The distinguished highest-weight vertex generating the sub-crystal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.member","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.member","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L180-L180","doc":"Membership predicate cutting out the Demazure sub-crystal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L178-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.DemazureSubcrystal","kind":"class","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L171-L193","doc":"Conditional class for Demazure module identification: a Demazure\nsub-crystal at level `level` corresponds to a Weyl-group word.  The\nsub-crystal is carried as a predicate `member` with a distinguished\nhighest-weight generator (`highest`, pinned by `highest_isHighest` as an\nactual highest-weight vertex — annihilated by every raising operator);\n`demazure_closure` states the defining Demazure property (closed under the\nfirst `level` lowering operators — the Weyl-word support). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.embed_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.embed_injective","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The embedding is injective — a genuine embedding, not just a\nmorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.embed","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The embedding as a crystal morphism (commutes with `f` and `e`).\n(Was the `True` field `sl_n_embedding`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.target","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L163-L163","doc":"The target crystal — a tensor power of the standard `sl_n` crystal\n(abstract datum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.TypeACrystal","kind":"class","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L153-L169","doc":"Conditional class for type-A specialisation: the crystal `G` embeds\ninto a tensor-power crystal of the standard `sl_n` representation.  The\ntarget crystal is abstract (the concrete standard-`sl_n` tensor-power\nconstruction is substantial and not in Mathlib); the class carries it as\na datum, `embed` as a genuine crystal morphism (`CrystalHom`, so the two\nmorphism laws are separate fields), and `embed_injective` making it a\ntrue *embedding*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instStembridgeCrystalStandardSl2Crystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instStembridgeCrystalStandardSl2Crystal","kind":"instance","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**`B(Λ₁)` is a genuine `StembridgeCrystal`** — a concrete,\nnon-trivial inhabitant of the reversibility axiom (unlike\n`trivialCrystal`, whose operators are all `none`).  The `f₀ : false ↦ true`\narrow and its `e₀`-inverse are mutually reversible; every other operator\nis `none` on both sides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal.reversibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal.reversibility","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L137-L137","doc":"The foundational Kashiwara crystal axiom presupposed by the full\nStembridge S1–S8: for every simple-root label `i`, the raising and\nlowering operators `e i`, `f i` are mutually inverse partial maps —\n`f i v = some w ↔ e i w = some v`.  (No longer `True`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StembridgeCrystal","kind":"class","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L122-L138","doc":"Conditional class carrying the foundational crystal axiom.\nNEAR-MATCH tier.  The reversibility field is inhabitable by a genuine\ncrystal — see the `standardSl2Crystal` instance below; the full\nStembridge S1–S8 instance still requires upstream Mathlib crystal-graph\nmachinery.\n\nThe single field encodes the Kashiwara **reversibility** law, *not* the\nfull Stembridge S1–S8 (whose additional string-length / interplay\nconditions would further constrain an instance) — hence the field is\nnamed `reversibility` rather than `stembridge_axioms`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.map_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.map_e","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L118-L118","doc":"`toFun` commutes with raising: `e i` then map = map then `e i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.map_f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.map_f","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L116-L116","doc":"`toFun` commutes with lowering: `f i` then map = map then `f i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.toFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.toFun","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The underlying vertex map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalHom","kind":"structure","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L109-L118","doc":"A **morphism of crystal graphs**: a vertex map `toFun` commuting with\nboth the lowering (`f`) and raising (`e`) operators.  Bundling the two\nmorphism laws as separate fields keeps downstream rewriting smooth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.standardSl2Crystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.standardSl2Crystal","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L98-L105","doc":"The **standard `sl₂` crystal** `B(Λ₁)`: two vertices — `false` = highest\nweight, `true` = lowest weight — joined by the single `f₀`-arrow\n`false ↦ true` (and its `e₀`-inverse `true ↦ false`). All other operators\nare `none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.trivialCrystal_unique_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.trivialCrystal_unique_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L89-L91","doc":"The trivial crystal has exactly one vertex (by `Unit` being a singleton). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.trivialCrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.trivialCrystal","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The **trivial crystal**: one vertex `unit`, both operators return `none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.e","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Raising operator `e i v` (Option-valued for partiality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.f","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Lowering operator `f i v` (Option-valued for partiality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.V","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The vertex set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CrystalGraph","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/KashiwaraCrystalBasic.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**Kashiwara crystal graph** structure: a type `V` of vertices,\nwith partial endomorphisms `f i : V → Option V` and `e i : V → Option V`\nindexed by simple-root labels `i : ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}